# .codedna — CodeDNA project manifest (auto-generated by codedna manifest)
project: codedna
description: "An In-Source Communication Protocol for AI Coding Agents — spec, benchmark, tools"

exclude:
  - "labs/benchmark/**"
  - "experiments/runs/**"
  - "benchmark_agent/runs/**"
  - "benchmark_agent/projects_swebench/**"

packages:
  (root):
    purpose: "analyze claude code test, benchmark server, status module"
    key_files: [run_agent_multi.py, parser.py, agent_history.py, order.rb, benchmark_server.py]

  benchmark_agent/projects_swebench/django__django-11808/:
    purpose: "config, registry, django-admin module"
    key_files: [utils.py, models.py, base.py, views.py, admin.py]

  benchmark_agent/projects_swebench/django__django-11991/:
    purpose: "config, registry, django-admin module"
    key_files: [utils.py, models.py, base.py, views.py, admin.py]

  benchmark_agent/projects_swebench/django__django-12508/:
    purpose: "config, registry, django-admin module"
    key_files: [utils.py, models.py, base.py, views.py, admin.py]

  benchmark_agent/projects_swebench/django__django-13495/:
    purpose: "config, registry, django-admin module"
    key_files: [utils.py, models.py, base.py, views.py, admin.py]

  benchmark_agent/projects_swebench/django__django-14480/:
    purpose: "config, registry, global settings module"
    key_files: [utils.py, models.py, base.py, admin.py, views.py]

  codedna_tool/:
    purpose: "cli, wiki module"
    key_files: [cli.py, wiki.py, __init__.py]
    depends_on: [codedna_tool/languages/]

  codedna_tool/languages/:
    purpose: " treesitter,  ts csharp,  ts go module"
    key_files: [base.py, _treesitter.py, __init__.py, java.py, go.py]

  examples/go-api/:
    purpose: "main module"
    key_files: [main.go]

  examples/go-api/handlers/:
    purpose: "revenue module"
    key_files: [revenue.go]

  examples/go-api/models/:
    purpose: "user module"
    key_files: [user.go]

  examples/go-api/services/:
    purpose: "revenue module"
    key_files: [revenue.go]

  examples/go-api/utils/:
    purpose: "format module"
    key_files: [format.go]

  tests/:
    purpose: "conftest, test cli, test integration langs module"
    key_files: [test_language_adapters.py, test_integration_langs.py, test_refresh.py, test_cli.py, test_validator.py]
    depends_on: [codedna_tool/, codedna_tool/languages/]

  tests/fixtures/:
    purpose: "user service, UserService, UserService module"
    key_files: [UserService.kt, user_service.rb, user_service.go, UserService.ts, UserService.java]

cross_cutting_patterns: {}

agent_sessions:
  - agent: "claude-opus-4-7"
    provider: "anthropic"
    date: "2026-05-01"
    session_id: "s_20260501_json_robust"
    task: "fix _parse_json_response for newer reasoning-style models (V4-Flash, R1, Qwen-thinking)"
    changed: ["codedna_tool/cli.py","tests/test_cli.py","CHANGELOG.md"]
    visited: ["codedna_tool/cli.py","tests/test_cli.py","CHANGELOG.md"]
    message: "The same user session that hit the skip-list drift also lost 46/47\nbatches because the LLM JSON parser only accepted strict JSON or\n```json fences at the very start of the response. Newer reasoning\nmodels (DeepSeek V4-Flash, R1, Qwen-thinking) routinely emit\nexplanatory prose before/after the JSON, or wrap reasoning in\n<think>...</think> tags, regardless of how strict the prompt is. Test-\nfirst: 11 tests probing every realistic shape — 4 of them were red on\npre-fix code (leading prose, trailing prose, thinking tags, fenced\nJSON with leading prose). Fix: new Strategy 3 in _parse_json_response\nuses json.JSONDecoder.raw_decode to scan every '{' index until one\nparses cleanly. Strategy ordering: (1) extract from any ``` fence,\n(2) direct parse, (3) raw_decode at every '{', (4) truncated repair\nvia last `\",`. Plus: env-gated raw-response logging\n(CODEDNA_DEBUG_LLM_RESPONSES=/path) so the next \"invalid JSON\"\nreporter gives us a sample without needing a debug build. Total: 218\npassed / 0 failed (was 207). Did NOT touch the prompt itself — fixing\nthe parser is more robust than chasing model-specific prompts."
  - agent: "claude-opus-4-7"
    provider: "anthropic"
    date: "2026-05-01"
    session_id: "s_20260501_codedna_exclude"
    task: "add project-wide exclude: field at .codedna top level"
    changed: ["codedna_tool/cli.py","tests/test_cli.py",".codedna"]
    visited: ["codedna_tool/cli.py","tests/test_cli.py",".codedna","CLAUDE.md","pyproject.toml"]
    message: "Driven by user frustration: `codedna manifest .` walked into\nlabs/benchmark/projects/ (vendored SWE-bench fixtures with LaTeX\nescapes \\\\Lambda and Win paths \\\\Documents) firing SyntaxWarning\non every ast.parse(). Pre-fix the only way to silence it was to\npass --exclude on every CLI invocation. Solution: top-level\n`exclude:` field in .codedna, supporting both YAML flow form\n`[a, b]` and block form `- a\\\\n- b`. Read by manifest, check,\nrefresh, and init via _read_codedna_excludes() and merged\nadditively with --exclude in main(). Round-trips through\n_read_existing_codedna → _write_codedna verbatim so manifest\nregeneration never silently drops the user's exclude. 5 regression\ntests in TestManifest (3 unit on _parse_exclude_field, 1 E2E, 1\nround-trip). All 7 TestManifest tests green; 5 pre-existing\nfailures (4 TestLLM monkeypatch on missing _litellm attribute, 1\nTestCodeDNAManifest missing PyYAML) confirmed pre-existing via\ngit stash before/after — not caused by this change.\nSide-quest in same session: bonified Python 3.14 brew bottle on\nmacOS Tahoe 26.2 (broken pyexpat — libexpat ABI mismatch),\nswitched to brew --build-from-source python@3.13 + pipx\nreinstall, set PIPX_DEFAULT_PYTHON in ~/.zshrc."
  - agent: "claude-opus-4-7"
    provider: "anthropic"
    date: "2026-05-02"
    session_id: "s_20260502_init_escapes_testdata"
    task: "fix #12 (init loses backslash escapes) and #13 (testdata not in skip list)"
    changed: ["codedna_tool/cli.py","tests/test_cli.py",".codedna"]
    visited: ["codedna_tool/cli.py","tests/test_cli.py","codedna_tool/wiki.py",".codedna"]
    message: "yuzi-co reported two more init regressions, both fixed in one shot.\n#12: scan_file used ast.get_docstring(tree) which returns the\n*evaluated* string — Python's parser had already collapsed\n`\\\\<newline>` line continuations and downgraded `\\\\\\\\` to `\\\\`.\nRound-tripping that into a rewritten docstring silently turned a\nrunnable shell example into a single concatenated command, and\ndowngraded ASCII pipeline diagrams (`\\\\\\\\->`) such that the next\nimport fired SyntaxWarning. Fix: new FileInfo.docstring_raw_body\nfield captured via ast.get_source_segment + strip surrounding\ntriple quotes + lstrip leading newlines (matches ast.get_docstring's\nsummary-on-line-0 convention). build_module_docstring prefers\ndocstring_raw_body over docstring; falls back if None (e.g.\nf-string Expr nodes). #13: added `testdata` to _DEFAULT_SKIP_DIRS\nnext to .claude / worktrees. Go's analysistest fixtures encode\nexpected diagnostic positions in `// want \"…\"` comments tied to\nspecific line numbers — header injection broke them. `go test`\nitself ignores testdata/ for build purposes, we follow the same\nconvention. wiki.SKIP_DIRS inherits via _DEFAULT_SKIP_DIRS so the\ndrift-guard test still passes. 3 regression tests in TestInit, all\ngreen. Full test_cli.py: 60 passed (was 57), 4 pre-existing\nfailures unrelated."
  - agent: "deepseek-v4-pro"
    provider: "deepseek"
    date: "2026-07-10"
    session_id: "s_20260710_docblock"
    task: "accept /** */ docblock CodeDNA headers; skip Laravel bootstrap/storage"
    changed: ["codedna_tool/cli.py","integrations/opencode-plugin/codedna.js","tools/validate_manifests.py","tools/pre-commit","tests/test_refresh.py","tests/test_cli.py","tests/test_validator.py",".codedna"]
    visited: ["codedna_tool/cli.py","codedna_tool/wiki.py","codedna_tool/languages/base.py","codedna_tool/languages/php.py","integrations/opencode-plugin/codedna.js","tools/validate_manifests.py","tests/test_refresh.py","tests/test_cli.py","tests/test_validator.py",".codedna"]
    message: "Vibe Bridge (Larens94/vibebridge) reported refresh + wiki bootstrap\nyielding 0 files on a Laravel 12 + React 19 project whose PHP/TSX files\ncarried CodeDNA headers in JSDoc/PHPDoc docblock form (/** ... */ with\neach line prefixed by *). Root cause: _parse_lang_header only stripped the\nlanguage comment_prefix (// #), so ` * exports:` never matched → returned\nNone. Since this parser is shared by cmd_refresh AND wiki._extract_fields,\na single fix repaired both. Header range now spans the /** opener through\nthe */ closer so _replace_lang_header rewrites the whole block cleanly\n(docblock normalises to canonical // on refresh — no field loss). Also\nadded Laravel bootstrap/ + storage/ to _DEFAULT_SKIP_DIRS (scaffolding +\nruntime, never source — inflated check coverage denominator; they reported\n280 files / 13%). OpenCode plugin fixes (real bugs from their report):\nclient.app.log now uses { body: { service, level, message } } not the\npositional form that silently no-ops; all hooks wrapped in try/catch;\nfilePath resolution falls back through file_path/path/fileName. Kept the\nplugin WARN-ONLY (tool.execute.after) — declined their block-on-write\nredesign (tool.execute.before + throw); hard enforcement belongs in the\npre-commit hook, and their edit false-positive was self-inflicted by the\nblock. Declined tools/refresh-wiki.py (redundant — wiki bootstrap already\ncovers every adapter language; their script hardcoded Laravel SCAN_DIRS).\n6 tests in TestDocblockHeader + skip-set asserts. E2E verified on a real\nLaravel+React fixture: check 3/3, refresh updates docblock preserving\nrules/agent, wiki bootstrap emits 2 pages, no vendor/node_modules/\nbootstrap/storage leakage, init idempotent on docblock files. Pre-existing\n5 failures (TestLLM litellm, TestCodeDNAManifest yaml) confirmed unrelated.\nAlso fixed two pre-existing bugs in tools/pre-commit surfaced while\ncommitting this work: (1) it mapped js/jsx/mjs → `ts` for `codedna check\n--extensions`, so `check file.js --extensions ts` counted 0 files and the\nblock-grep on \"L1 (module headers) 0/\" mis-read that as a missing header —\nEVERY .js/.jsx commit was blocked. Now each extension passes through as-is.\n(2) the block signal itself was wrong: \"L1 (module headers) X/Y\" counts\nPython files ONLY (always 0/0 for non-Python), so it can't indicate a\nmissing non-Python header. Switched to `check --verbose` and block only on\nthe \"Missing L1:\" / \"Missing non-Python L1:\" markers, which list genuinely\nun-annotated files. Refresh re-stage loop now re-stages ALL staged source\nfiles, not just .py (refresh rewrites non-Python headers too). Reinstalled\n.git/hooks/pre-commit from tools/pre-commit."
  - agent: "gpt-5"
    provider: "openai"
    date: "2026-08-20"
    session_id: "s_20260820_sessions"
    task: "robust manifest session retention"
    changed: ["codedna_tool/manifest_store.py","codedna_tool/cli.py","tests/test_manifest_store.py","tests/test_cli.py","tests/test_refresh.py","tests/test_wiki.py","tests/__init__.py","codedna_tool/languages/csharp.py","pyproject.toml",".gitignore","AGENTS.md","CLAUDE.md","SPEC.md","integrations/copilot-instructions.md","integrations/.windsurfrules",".codedna"]
    visited: [".codedna","docs/wiki/cli.md","codedna_tool/cli.py","pyproject.toml","tests/test_cli.py","tests/test_validator.py","AGENTS.md","CLAUDE.md","SPEC.md","integrations/copilot-instructions.md","integrations/.windsurfrules"]
    message: "Implemented locked atomic session retention, canonical append/prune commands, lossless manifest section updates, YAML-safe serialization, and concurrency regression coverage. Git remains the complete audit log."
